1
00:00:01,050 --> 00:00:06,575
Briefing for energy ministries, regulators and procurement units. Filter at the gate.

2
00:00:09,675 --> 00:00:13,792
Minister Kerbu: A developer brought us this proposal directly. They can sign next week.

3
00:00:14,092 --> 00:00:17,762
Belpau: Then we test it against the least-cost plan before anything is signed.

4
00:00:19,512 --> 00:00:32,312
The World Bank's guidelines warn that unsolicited proposals often run into trouble, among other things by diverting public resources away from the strategic plans of the government.

5
00:00:35,562 --> 00:00:48,106
Nigeria's solar tariff was set administratively, before any competitive price discovery. When solar costs fell, the government tried to reopen it, and the programme stalled over the dispute.

6
00:00:51,156 --> 00:01:02,249
An MoU is cheap to obtain and valuable to hold. In Nigeria, some local developers were reportedly waiting to sell their projects to international firms.

7
00:01:05,299 --> 00:01:10,014
Decision note. Is this project needed, and could a competition beat it?

8
00:01:10,914 --> 00:01:15,820
Unsolicited proposals bypass planning, price discovery and scrutiny.

9
00:01:16,270 --> 00:01:19,001
A published tariff becomes the benchmark.

10
00:01:19,451 --> 00:01:23,355
And exclusivity without progress blocks better projects.

11
00:01:23,805 --> 00:01:30,077
Your decision: test any MoU outside the least-cost plan against the plan, before it is signed.

12
00:01:31,277 --> 00:01:40,173
Compete by default. Attach milestones, sunset clauses and development securities. And keep and publish the MoU register.

13
00:01:42,623 --> 00:01:43,306
Stop.

14
00:01:43,806 --> 00:01:45,619
You head the procurement unit.

15
00:01:46,119 --> 00:01:50,471
An unsolicited proposal promises power in eighteen months.

16
00:01:50,871 --> 00:01:53,623
Its indicative tariff looks attractive.

17
00:01:54,023 --> 00:01:56,818
It asks for five years of exclusivity.

18
00:01:57,218 --> 00:01:58,562
What do you recommend?

19
00:02:05,762 --> 00:02:08,471
Discover the price before you print it.

20
00:02:10,521 --> 00:02:11,908
Filter at the gate.

21
00:02:12,808 --> 00:02:15,752
Every published number becomes a benchmark.
